# Web UI build output
#
# hermes_cli/web_dist/ used to be TRACKED so a fresh clone could run
# `argus dashboard --skip-build` with no Node toolchain.  That stopped paying
# for itself once the dashboard was code-split: one bundle became ~55 hashed
# chunks, so every frontend change rewrote the whole set and buried real diffs
# in generated noise.  Every file in it is reproducible byte-for-byte from
# `cd web && npm run build` (verified: identical content hashes, fonts/webp
# included, sourced from web/public/ + the @nous-research/ui package).
#
# Nothing needs it committed any more:
#   - `argus dashboard` / `argus update` build it automatically (only
#     --skip-build opts out, and it errors loudly if the dist is absent —
#     hermes_cli/main.py:11769)
#   - `scripts/release.py` builds it before `uv build`, so wheels still ship
#     a fresh dashboard via the pyproject package-data entry
#   - the Docker image builds its own copy (and .dockerignore now excludes
#     this path so `COPY . .` can't clobber it)
#
# The non-generated sources live in web/public/ and stay tracked.
hermes_cli/web_dist/
apps/desktop/build/
apps/desktop/dist/
apps/desktop/release/
apps/desktop/*.tsbuildinfo

# Web UI assets — synced from @nous-research/ui at build time via
# `npm run sync-assets` (see web/package.json).
web/public/fonts/
web/public/ds-assets/

