# ── In-repo runtime state (never source) ─────────────────────────────────────
# When the agent/gateway runs inside this checkout instead of ~/.hermes, it
# writes its live state here. These are 59 MB in aggregate and MUST stay
# ignored: `argus update` runs `git stash push --include-untracked`, so any
# untracked payload gets swept into a stash together with real uncommitted
# work (see the .hermes-bootstrap-complete note above for the same hazard).
#
# state.db also carries conversation content and sessions/ holds raw request
# dumps — both are private data that must never reach the remote.
state.db
state.db-journal
state.db-wal
state.db-shm
verification_evidence.db
sessions/
cache/
.update_check
auth.lock

# Cron scheduler state: user-created jobs with their prompts (private) plus the
# scheduler's own lock. `cron/` is runtime state written by the cron engine.
cron/jobs.json
cron/.jobs.lock

# Skills runtime bookkeeping — usage counters and the bundled-skill manifest are
# regenerated on demand, unlike the tracked skills/<name>/ source dirs.
skills/.usage.json
skills/.usage.json.lock
skills/.bundled_manifest

# Vendored native helper binary (18 MB, arm64 Mach-O) — a build/install output,
# not source. Fetched per-platform rather than committed.
bin/tirith

# ★ Demo videos (too large for GitHub, hosted as Release Assets on argus-public)
# .mov 是原始高清 (>100MB), 走 GitHub Release Assets
demos/*.mov
# .mp4 是压缩后 (~10-30MB), 直接 track 到 repo 供内嵌播放
